[mssql] plain explain: EXPLAIN SELECT a FROM t => |ro=run rw=run full=run|
[mssql] empty:  => |ro=refuse(NoStatement) rw=refuse(NoStatement) full=refuse(NoStatement)|
[mssql] whitespace only:     => |ro=refuse(NoStatement) rw=refuse(NoStatement) full=refuse(NoStatement)|
[mssql] line comment only: -- nothing => |ro=refuse(NoStatement) rw=refuse(NoStatement) full=refuse(NoStatement)|
[mssql] block comment only: /* x */ => |ro=refuse(NoStatement) rw=refuse(NoStatement) full=refuse(NoStatement)|
[mssql] two reads: SELECT 1; SELECT 2 => |ro=refuse(MoreThanOne) rw=refuse(MoreThanOne) full=refuse(MoreThanOne)|
[mssql] two drops: DROP TABLE a; DROP TABLE b => |ro=refuse(MoreThanOne) rw=refuse(MoreThanOne) full=refuse(MoreThanOne)|
[mssql] read then garbage: SELECT 1; garbage => |ro=refuse(Unreadable) rw=refuse(Unreadable) full=refuse(Unreadable)|
[mssql] a typo: selec 1 => |ro=refuse(Unreadable) rw=refuse(Unreadable) full=refuse(Unreadable)|
[mssql] read, then a line comment: SELECT 1; -- c => |ro=run rw=run full=run|
[mssql] line comment, then a read: -- c\u{a}SELECT 1 => |ro=run rw=run full=run|
[mssql] block comment, then a read: /* c */ SELECT 1 => |ro=run rw=run full=run|
[mssql] read, then a hash comment: SELECT 1 # c => |ro=refuse(Unreadable) rw=refuse(Unreadable) full=refuse(Unreadable)|
